.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Raw historical data collected by training/data/collect_gamelogs.py.
# Large, regenerable from stats.nba.com, and specific to whoever ran the
# collector -- see training/data/README.md for how to regenerate it.
training/data/raw/

# Processed V1 feature panel built by training/dataset.py -- regenerable
# from the raw data above via `python -m training.dataset build`.
training/data/processed/

# Training-side model registry (models/registry/<version>/), built by
# training/train.py. This is NOT models/points_regression.pkl (the
# deployed legacy model, which stays committed as-is) and is not read by
# any production code path. The large, regenerable binaries (model.pkl,
# ~35MB; residuals.parquet, ~1MB) are gitignored -- rerun
# `python -m training.train` to reproduce them from the same panel/seed.
# metadata.json/metrics.json/feature_importances.json are small,
# human-readable, and deliberately NOT ignored, so a version's config,
# scores, and feature ranking are reviewable in git history even though
# the binary artifact itself isn't committed.
models/registry/*/model.pkl
models/registry/*/residuals.parquet

# CURRENT_V1 is a machine-local pointer to whichever version's model.pkl
# happens to exist on this machine. Since model.pkl itself is gitignored
# above, committing this pointer would let a clean clone see a named
# "current" version whose actual model artifact was never shipped --
# an apparently-usable registry that silently isn't. It stays local-only
# until a later step introduces real artifact storage (e.g. an artifact
# store/registry service) where a committed pointer would resolve to
# something that actually exists for everyone. Run `python -m
# training.train` locally to (re)create both the version directory and
# this pointer together.
models/registry/CURRENT_V1

# Step 5 experiment outputs (training/experiments/results/<run_id>/,
# development-only, entirely separate from models/registry/ above and
# never read by any production code path). The only large binary is the
# final selected candidate's model, persisted at most once per run for
# convenience -- gitignored for the same reason as model.pkl above.
# search_results/ablation_results/validation_comparison/
# experiment_metadata are small JSON/CSV and deliberately committed so a
# run's search space, ablation results, and selected configuration stay
# reviewable in git history.
training/experiments/results/*/selected_candidate_model.pkl

# Step 8: local-only prediction board snapshots
# (src/services/persistence.py::save_board_snapshot). NOT the
# recommended production persistence shape (see that module's
# docstring for the prediction_runs/prediction_snapshots design) -- just
# a throwaway local artifact used to prove the board end-to-end. Never
# read by any app code.
data/prediction_snapshots/
